                        <field name="dc_description">A compendium of 39 medical texts by known and unknown authors, produced in the second half of the 9th century, most likely in northern Italy, already obtained at an early date by the Abbey Library of St. Gall. This codex includes—sometimes in unique exemplars—an alphabetically ordered Greek-Latin herbal glossary, the treatise "De re medica" by one Pseudo-Plinius (Physica Plinii), and a longer medical tract entitled "Liber Esculapii". </field>
